    "body": "Detect runtime/doc/*.txt patches that only modify date AND modify N/A Vimscript functions as N/A.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n## Problem:\r\nIt's not enough to detect N/A patches even I list all N/A Vimscript functions. Need to modify `xfuncname` which means modifying `.gitattributes` or passing inline config (if possible?) to detect Ex commands, options. Also, `{` is incompatible with `-I` flag so I cannot remove hunks that modify `available when compiled with` . May need many backslashes, `\\`  , to ensure `{` and similar characters are escaped.\r\n\r\nWait, I got 1\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim-patch:9ade3f589 runtime(doc): Clarification in listener_add() doc\r\n```",
